<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
    <string>ai.hippocampus</string>
    <key>CFBundleName</key>
    <string>Hippocampus</string>
    <key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
    <string>Hippocampus</string>
    <key>CFBundleExecutable</key>
    <string>Hippocampus</string>
    <key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
    <string>0.1.0</string>
    <key>CFBundleVersion</key>
    <string>1</string>
    <key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
    <string>APPL</string>
    <key>CFBundleIconFile</key>
    <string>AppIcon</string>
    <key>CFBundleIconName</key>
    <string>AppIcon</string>
    <key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key>
    <string>14.0</string>
    <key>LSUIElement</key>
    <true/>
    <key>NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Hippocampus records your screen to build your private, searchable brain. All processing happens on-device.</string>
    <key>NSAccessibilityUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Hippocampus uses Accessibility to detect password fields and secure input, so it can automatically stop capturing when you type sensitive information.</string>
    <key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Hippocampus reads the URL of your active browser tab so your brain knows what page you were looking at. No page content is sent anywhere.</string>
    <key>NSCalendarsUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Hippocampus reads your current calendar event so each captured moment is tagged with "what meeting was happening right now." Only events whose time window covers right now are read; no past events, no event bodies, no attendee lists leave your Mac.</string>
    <key>NSContactsUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Hippocampus resolves the people who appear in your captured context to a stable contact identifier so your brain can answer "who was I talking to" later. Only the matching contact's identifier is stored; names, phone numbers, emails, and photos never leave your Mac.</string>
    <key>NSAppleMusicUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Hippocampus reads the title and artist of whatever is currently playing on this Mac so each captured moment is tagged with "what was I listening to." Only the currently-playing title and artist are read; no library, no playlists, no purchase history.</string>
    <key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>CFBundleURLName</key>
            <string>ai.hippocampus.recall</string>
            <key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
            <array>
                <string>hippocampus</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
    <!-- Sparkle 2.x auto-update configuration.
         Feed URL is co-hosted with the DMG on the Vercel landing surface
         until the `hippocampus.ai` custom domain is provisioned (OWNER_TASKS #3);
         at that point the URL flips to https://appcast.hippocampus.ai/appcast.xml
         per docs/appcast-hosting.md, and Sparkle picks it up on the next reship.
         SUPublicEDKey is a placeholder Ed25519 public key — Amy runs
         scripts/sparkle-keygen.sh (OWNER_TASKS #4) to mint the real keypair,
         which replaces this string. The placeholder means unsigned builds
         will fetch the feed but reject any <item> until the real key is
         wired — deliberate; keeps the pipeline testable end-to-end without
         shipping trust before the key is in 1Password. -->
    <key>SUFeedURL</key>
    <string>https://hippocampus-swart.vercel.app/appcast.xml</string>
    <key>SUPublicEDKey</key>
    <string>XRC6iJSDpOpPuA78CqB0vC6Lw1YUyZalLIXgyBCfG00=</string>
    <key>SUEnableSystemProfiling</key>
    <false/>
    <key>SUEnableInstallerLauncher</key>
    <true/>
    <key>SUEnableAutomaticChecks</key>
    <true/>
    <key>SUAutomaticallyUpdate</key>
    <false/>
    <key>SUScheduledCheckInterval</key>
    <integer>86400</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
